**Recommendation: confirmatory, family of four, confined to the §5 test; everything else exploratory.** Reasoning: §5's claim is already published unqualified, and an exploratory test of a published claim cannot discharge it. But nothing else in E2 has a discovery sample — `EXPERIMENTS.md` predicts nothing — so freezing point predictions we don't have would be theatre. Family = Qwen NATIVE, two-sided AWARE−PLACEBO at de/th × {1024, 2048}, Holm at α=0.05. Non-binding cells chosen by a *measured* pre-stated criterion (E1 censoring < 2%), which excludes Qwen Swahili — still 10–11% censored at 2048. Added a manipulation-check gate: a null is uninterpretable unless AWARE demonstrably shifts length at binding budgets. The all-exploratory alternative is argued in §8.5.

